{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792306643,"nonce":"+6M+WqU8LS4M5lahjSkMLSL2gMA=","title":"Blinc DSL as a blinc_abi language SDK, rendered by blinc_gpu: what moves, what stays","message":"Evaluation, not a plan: nothing here is decided. Facts are marked measured (run or counted here) or read (from source, not run). Related: 6f7b001 (engine model), 2c565dc (retire stateful), a33d2b9 (imported view instance id).\n\n\nWhat blinc_abi is now (read, counted)\n\nAbout 33.6k lines in src including tests, up from the 6k in 6f7b001. Three layers matter here.\n- graph.rs: GraphContext wraps blinc_core's ReactiveGraph with unit-valued signals and computeds. Values stay in the host language. Host effects run their body in the host and report their reads (begin_effect, end_effect_with_reads), so a host that tracks its own reads can feed the graph.\n- context.rs, scene.rs, hit.rs, text.rs: LayoutContext owns a Taffy tree plus blinc_layout RenderProps per node; SceneEncoder walks it into display-list records; hit_test returns the nodes under a point; text.rs gives measurement and caret positions.\n- css/: parser, arena stylesheet, compiled form, cascade over a Tree trait, 12.4k non-test lines. Blinc's own blinc_css is 20.8k. Two CSS engines now exist.\n\nWhat it does not do: event dispatch, focus, keyboard and text-field editing, scroll physics, overlays, transitions and motion. Each SDK writes those. blinc_ts does it in about 23.4k lines of TypeScript (its DOM-like Host) plus about 4.7k for motion; ashui in about 43k lines of Haxe plus 7.5k of components. The README says as much: language SDKs supply components and renderer orchestration. The host interface blinc_ts documents (createElement, setProperty, bindProperty, insertBefore, addEventListener) names \"a hand-written DSL\" as an intended client.\n\n\nMeasured: it builds and runs inside this workspace\n\nblinc_abi (default-features = false, features = [\"scene\"]) resolves against the local crates with a [patch.\"https://github.com/project-blinc/blinc\"] table pointing at crates/*. Without the patch cargo links two copies of blinc_layout, blinc_core, blinc_css and others; with it, `cargo tree -d` shows none. A scratch program created a LayoutContext, a flex node with a background and 12px radius and a text child, ran compute, then SceneEncoder::prepare and read. Result: bounds as expected, 6 records (one PRIM_RECT with radii 12 and the fill colour, five PRIM_TEXT glyph quads). No HashLink, Node or xgpu involved. Rendering was not run.\n\n\nWhere the DSL is coupled today (counted)\n\n- WidgetBox is Text | Div | Custom(Box\u003cdyn ElementBuilder\u003e): every DSL view value is a blinc_layout builder.\n- 120 host builtins in abi.rs; widget_ffi.rs is 1.7k lines; blinc_cn_dsl wraps 127 cn widgets in 8.1k lines.\n- Re-rendering is rebuild: `with` regions mount a Stateful (with_regions.rs), @stateful wraps a view, call-site ids (current_call_id) key per-instance state.\n- Signals cross as Reactive\u003cT\u003e = Literal | Signal | Computed with the signal token as payload. That is the same shape as ashui's IntoReactive\u003cT\u003e and blinc_ts's bindProperty(name, signal).\nThe grammar (2.7k lines) and the Zyntax passes do not name blinc_layout; the extern layer does.\n\n\nThe rendering seam is the hard part\n\nblinc_abi's display list is not GpuPrimitive. Records are 112 floats (28 vec4 rows); GpuPrimitive is 24 vec4 (96 floats). Rows 0 to 15 map almost field for field (bounds, radii, fill, gradient end, border, shadow, clip, gradient params, corner shape, type info). The record adds per-side border colours, a second (local) clip, overflow-fade rects, a clip-path frame and shape, 3-stop gradient tables, and layer and backdrop records. GpuPrimitive has what the record lacks: 3D (perspective, sdf_3d, light), CSS filter rows and mask gradients. blinc_abi's CSS has no shape-3d, perspective or 3d-op. So the contract has diverged in both directions, and Blinc's 3D-SDF CSS has no ABI form.\n\nThree ways to keep blinc_gpu as the renderer.\nR1. Consume the records in a new blinc_gpu module: records to GpuPrimitive, glyph quads sampled from the encoder's own atlas (read_atlas, revisioned uploads), images and canvases through slots. One paint-walk semantic shared with ashui and blinc_ts, so the same scene gives the same pixels everywhere. The missing rows become blinc_gpu shader work or an approximation. blinc_ts's equivalent consumer is only about 950 lines of TypeScript plus shaders.\nR2. A second walk in Blinc that emits blinc_core DrawContext calls from the ABI tree. DrawContext already has fill_rect_with_per_side_border, set_overflow_fade, set_corner_shape, set_css_filter, set_mask_gradient, push_layer, so every Blinc GPU feature stays reachable. Cost: a second copy of a 3.2k-line walk, and pixels can drift from the other SDKs. blinc_abi would also need to expose its tree read-only.\nR3 (orthogonal): do not build a new app shell. A leaf element, like canvas, owns an ABI LayoutContext and SceneEncoder, paints through R1 or R2 and forwards pointer and key events to hit_test. Existing windows, overlays and motion keep working around it.\n\n\nWhat the DSL would lower to\n\n- signal: value in the Zyntax handler (as today's design), a GraphContext signal key as the token. computed and effect: GraphContext computed and host effects with the closure run by Zyntax.\n- view elements: create_node or create_text, typed props through LayoutContext::apply and set_properties, classes and attributes for the cascade. Bound props become one effect per property, not an overlay plus a rebuild.\n- for, match, with: region components (insert_before, detach, remove under an owner) instead of Stateful. That retires with_regions.rs's Stateful mount.\n- events: hit_test then DSL closures. Focus, keyboard and text-field policy needs a host layer (see below).\n- fsm: unchanged, logic only; reaches CSS as an attribute.\n- hot reload: dispose the root scope and remount on the same host, which is blinc_ts's HMR model.\n- identity: component bodies run once, so call-site ids and the instance-id plumbing (a33d2b9) should not be needed. Inferred, not checked.\n\n\nDecisions that are the owner's\n\n1. Route. A: DSL becomes a third ABI SDK, cn is rewritten as DSL components plus CSS (ashui's shape). B: keep blinc_layout as the engine and finish 6f7b001 steps 1 to 4, no ABI dependency. C: define a DSL host interface (create, set, bind with Reactive\u003cT\u003e tokens, insert, listen, dispose), implement it over today's blinc_layout first, then over the ABI, and compare pixels. C keeps cn and Rust widgets working through the move and makes A or B a later choice, but the blinc_layout implementation only supports in-place updates as far as 6f7b001 gets.\n2. Behaviour layer. Written once in Rust and shared (blinc_ts and ashui each re-implement the same DOM-like behaviours in their own language), written in the DSL, or reused from blinc_layout's event router and text input. The reuse option is bound to Div and RenderTree today.\n3. Who owns the pixel contract: records as the truth (R1) or Blinc's DrawContext (R2).\n4. Dependency direction. blinc_abi depends on Blinc by git URL, so Blinc depending on blinc_abi is a URL cycle that only the [patch] table resolves. CI strips that block in some paths (see the gpu-alloc note in the root Cargo.toml). Either blinc_abi becomes a workspace member or the patch stays on CI.\n5. Two CSS engines (blinc_css and blinc_abi/css) and which one a DSL scene uses.\n\n\nNot established\n\nAnything drawn: no pixels were produced through blinc_gpu. Event routing and focus through the ABI tree. How much of cn the ABI path can express (3D, mask gradients and custom GPU passes have no ABI form). Performance. Whether the ABI's CSS covers the properties cn_demo's theme depends on.\n\n\nSuggested order, each step landing alone\n\n1. The host interface, implemented over the current widget path, with the 120 builtins moved behind it. No behaviour change; the DSL suite is the gate.\n2. An ABI-backed implementation, headless: tree, props, signals, effects, regions, disposal. Gate: the same DSL programs give the same tree and records.\n3. R1 for the subset the spike produced (fill, radius, border, shadow, gradient, clip, text, images), offscreen, compared with the same scene through the current path.\n4. R3, the scene leaf in a blinc_app window, with pointer and key forwarding.\n5. The behaviour layer and cn, after decision 2.","files":null}]}